    "catalogDescription": "The Bachelor of Science in Biomedical Sciences is a broadly interdisciplinary degree, drawing on knowledge from both science and engineering. Students take a common set of core courses from several disciplines. For more in-depth study, they select an option in Biology, Chemistry, or Psychology & Neuroscience along with a concentration in one of four engineering fields: Biochemical Engineering, Bioinformatics, Biomaterials Engineering or Biomechanical Engineering.\n",
    "catalogDisplayName": "B.S. in Biomedical Sciences",
